# Enable BUILD_RT_DISCOVER at build time, then load rt_discover.fdx with this
# file as its configuration. Discovery is disabled unless explicitly loaded.
#
# Each Realm is an exact, case-insensitive Diameter realm, not a suffix or
# wildcard. List every peer identity that is authorized for that realm.
# DNS records alone do not authorize a peer: the peer must also authenticate
# using the configured TLS credentials and trust anchors. Its certificate must
# cover the authorized Origin-Host, queried realm, SRV target and
# certificate-eligible names encountered during DNS resolution.
# Optional peer settings apply to all discoveries for the realm:
# No_IP, No_IPv6, No_TCP, No_SCTP, Prefer_TCP, TcTimer, TwTimer,
# TLS_Prio and Realm (the expected Origin-Realm, independent of the query
# realm). Prefer_TCP is already the discovery default. No_TCP requires
# DTLS/SCTP. Port, ConnectTo and transport security mode are determined by
# DNS; TLS_old_method, No_TLS and SctpSec3436 are not supported.
#
# Realm = "example.org" {
#     Peer = "diameter1.example.org";
#     Peer = "diameter2.example.org";
#     TcTimer = 60;
#     TwTimer = 30;
#     No_SCTP;
#     TLS_Prio = "NORMAL";
#     Realm = "origin.example.org";
# };
#
# Discovery is attempted only when normal routing has no usable candidate.
# At most 256 requests may wait for discovery, and at most 64 distinct
# realm/application operations are retained until extension unload. An
# operation is created only after a routing request supplies its application.
# Requests wait at most 10 seconds, including any time in retry backoff; an
# expired request returns UNABLE_TO_DELIVER and is not retried.
# Existing static peers or peers owned by another discovery are not reused.
# After an initial failure, unexpected disconnect or failed TTL refresh, the
# extension stops the failed operation and retries in the background, even
# without waiting requests. Once stop completes, the delay starts at the
# realm's TcTimer, or 30 seconds if unset. It doubles after consecutive
# failures, adds 0 to floor(25%) seconds of random jitter, and is capped at
# 300 seconds or TcTimer, whichever is greater. A successful connection
# resets the delay. Incoming requests never accelerate a scheduled retry.
# If a peer disconnects with BUSY or DO_NOT_WANT_TO_TALK_TO_YOU, the
# realm/application operation is stopped and automatic discovery for that
# pair is suppressed until the extension is unloaded and reloaded. Waiting
# requests fail without a routing retry; later requests are not queued.
# Failed stops and stop-thread creation or join failures are logged and
# retried every second without restarting discovery; pending requests still
# expire. Shutdown drains requests and waits for every stop and join to
# succeed, so a persistent failure prevents unload. No new discovery attempts
# start during shutdown.
